    "chapter": "Playing the Game",
    "section": "1.40",
    "heading": "Ability Checks",
    "lineStart": 393,
    "lineEnd": 397
  },
  "section": "1.40",
  "rulesText": "Ability checks can be key in determining the outcome of a social interaction. Your roleplaying efforts can alter an NPC's attitude, but there might still be an element of chance if the GM wants dice to play a role in determining an NPC's response to you. In such situations, the GM will typically ask you to take the Influence action.\n\nPay attention to your skill proficiencies when thinking of how you will interact with an NPC; use an approach that relies on your group's skill proficiencies. For example, if the group needs to trick a guard into letting them into a castle, the Rogue who is proficient in Deception should lead the discussion."
}
